                    <occupation>OCCUPATION</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Wife of William Nicholson, and mother to their many children (for whom
                            there is a separate entry). Born Catherine Bouillie (25 March 1760, in
                            London), we know little about her, as yet. Godwin sees her on a number
                            of occasions without her husband, perhaps attempting to help while
                            Nicholson's debts forced him into the Fleet prison and to the King's
                            bench - in 1806-8. Nicholson died in May 1815, Godwin calls on Mrs
                            Nicholson (the last entry) some two weeks later, after he has called on
                            some of Nicholson's children. </p>
                    </note>
